On Oct 8, 10:51 am, Krzysiek <k...@wp.pl> wrote:
> Hello,
>
> How to define the lowest process ID which will be starts number processes for users ?
> Is this a kernel parameter ?
>
> Example : init process has ID 1
> Next process ID for user will be 1000 and over ......
>
> Regards,
> Chris

Next process ID is 2.  When the system boots, PIDs are numerically
sequential.  As startup processes die, the PID goes away.  Depending
on how many startup processes run, what data is in printer queues (lpd/
CUPS/lpdNG all startup processes), etc., this determines what PID the
first logon process will get.  Why does it matter?  What use can it
be?

-- robert



