> 
> The problem is as follows:
> I have a DS10 running tru64 V5.1 2650 as a webserver (installed by
> somebody who is not around anymore).  Computers running windows and some
> (!) linux machines have no problem accessing that server, but for most
> linux machines - weather on the same switch or over the internet - it is
> practically unreachable.
> Trying to connect via ssh runs fine (SYN,ACK) until my client gives the
> protocol, then I see only TCP retransmissions and previous segment
> losts. The server log just shows:
> 
> Oct 15 16:26:05 xxx sshd2[1209]: connection from "xxx.xxx.xxx.xxx" Oct
> 15 16:26:49 xxx sshd2[2102]: Local disconnected: Connection closed.
> 
> Same for http (from time to time a packet makes it through). Since the
> working linux clients are always the same, I looked in /etc/ hosts and
> /etc/resolv.conf - fine.
> 
> Any idea where to look?
> 
> Many thanks,
> Bjoern

Find out what the speed and duplex settings are for this port
on the switch side and set your Tru64 NIC speed to match (don't
set it to auto-negotiate)
You can do this with ifconfig, lanconfig or hwmgr in unix
Set it at the SRM console prompt to make it persistent
across reboots. Depending on your card type this will be a 
variable that starts with ewa or eia.



