Tru64 will do a reverse lookup (IP address -> Name) for incoming TCP
connections.
If there is no response from the DNS servers you have listed in /etc/
resolv.conf for such a lookup, this
can make your incoming connection appear to be very slow, or hang, or
be unusable, depending on
the service being offered.

You can check this on your Tru64 box by doing (say) nslookup w.x.y.z
for IP addresses of machines that work and don't work. If this is
indeed the issue, you may want to make sure that all your client
machines are either listed in /etc/hosts
(assuming you have "files" set to be the first lookup for "hosts" in /
etc/nsswitch.conf (or "local" in /etc/svc.conf)), or have
reverse lookups properly configured and findable by whatever DNS
servers you have listed in /etc/resolv.conf.

